course: dictionary
lesson: 15488
title: Structural: the parts that hold things up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Structural is about structure, which means how the parts of something are built, joined and organised. Think of your skeleton: it is the frame that holds your body up. Structural parts are the parts that hold a thing together.
explain: «The engineers checked the structural beams before the bridge opened.» The beams are the main frame that holds the bridge up, so they are structural parts. Without them, the bridge would fall down.
explain: «After the storm, the inspectors found structural damage to the roof.» Structural damage means the main frame has been harmed, so the building may not be safe. A scratch on the paint is not structural damage, because the frame is still strong.
explain: Structural can also describe a text. «The text has clear structural features: headings, paragraphs and a short summary.» Here the structure is the way the text is organised. When you meet structural, ask: is this about how something is built or joined?
fact: Structure means the way something is built or organised.
fact: Structural means to do with that structure, such as the frame or the parts that hold something up.
fact: Structural damage means harm to the main frame of a building or object, which can make it unsafe.
fact: Triangles are strong structural shapes, which is why they are often used in bridges and towers.
fact: In English, the structural features of a text are its headings, paragraphs and order.
exercise: «After the storm, the inspectors found structural damage to the roof.» What does structural mean here? | Something to do with the people inside | Something to do with how loud the wind was | *Something to do with the main frame that holds the roof up | Something to do with the colour of the paint
exercise: Which of these is a structural part of a bridge? | A traffic sign | *A steel beam | Its paint colour | A street lamp
exercise: Which of these is a structural feature of a text? | Its font colour | *Its headings and paragraphs | Its cover picture | Its smell
test: «After the earthquake, the inspectors looked for structural damage before anyone went back inside.» What does this tell you about structural damage? | The people's feelings are hurt | The colour of the walls has changed | *The main frame may be harmed, so the building could be unsafe | Only the garden is affected
test: Which shape is strong and often used as a structural shape in bridges? | Circle | *Triangle | Heart | Star
exam: Ella says structural just means strong. Which answer is best? | *Structural means to do with how the parts of something are built, joined or organised | Structural means very small | Structural means strong only, and nothing else | Structural means the same as colourful
